From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:48:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: 3D scene at a reduced resolution, writing at full
 size

Pi test of m2-3: the writing was sharp at 960x540 but only 5 fps. On
software OpenGL (RISC OS, or TORCS_SOFTWARE_GL), Graphic Configuration
has "Scene resolution (%)" (graph.xml "scene scale", a fraction;
default 100%). Below 100%, cGrScreen::update draws the 3D scene in the
bottom-left part of the screen's viewport (viewport and scissor scaled,
so the clears cover only that part too), copies it into a texture and
draws it over the whole viewport as one textured quad (one RGBA
power-of-two texture, GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE, GL_LINEAR, GL_REPLACE: Mesa's
fast textured-triangle path), then the mirror and the race display at the
full size. At 50% the scene has a quarter of the pixels. refresh()
leaves the full-screen clear to each screen when the scene is reduced.
Host (xlib swrast, 960x540, alone on forza): 17.6 fps at 100%, 26.7 at
50%.
---
 src/interfaces/graphic.h                  |  1 +
 src/libs/confscreens/graphconfig.cpp      | 29 ++++++++
 src/modules/graphic/ssggraph/grmain.cpp   | 12 +++
 src/modules/graphic/ssggraph/grmain.h     |  1 +
 src/modules/graphic/ssggraph/grscreen.cpp | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 133 insertions(+)

